        "abstract": "The purpose of this project is to design and build a monitoring device for data collection in the ocean. The goal of this project is to provide meaningful data concerning climate change. The sensors chosen were pH, temperature, dissolved oxygen, and pressure sensors. We designed a water-tight vessel to house the electronics. The vessel can log data for the trip and communicate with the X2nSat communication device as provided by the competition. In order to accomplish the objectives, we conducted research to mimic similar situations with underwater testing and computational simulations. We also tested different ways to communicate with the electronics within our device. Additionally, we explored the methods for which we would keep the device underwater. With testing, we were able to prove that we had created a functioning device capable of tracking the data we were interested in.",
