        "abstract": "Papers presented at this conference are the result of participation in the 2021 WERC Environmental Design Contest hosted by the Engineering New Mexico Resource Network, College of Engineering, New Mexico State University. Now in its 31st year, the Design Contest is modeled after an engineering RFP, challenging college teams to solve problems in emerging areas of environmental concern. Teams submit a technical report, give an oral presentation, present a conference-style poster, and demonstrate a working bench-scale model of their design. WERC independently tests all results during the contest, and judges are professional engineers who share a wealth of expertise with the contestants. The COVID-19 pandemic limited laboratory access for some teams, leading to paper studies. Other teams were able to build full bench-scale models of their designs. The papers presented in these proceedings are the result of both paper studies and bench-scale studies. Twenty one teams competed in the design contest. Of those teams, judges recommended eleven technical reports to be considered for publication. From that subset, a group of eight papers underwent a second review process and were determined to be eligible for publication.",
